{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.NuclearKnotClassification","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.NuclearKnotClassification","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Torsion.HeckeMassElement","lean:module:QOU.Torsion.TopologicalMass"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.nuclear_knot_classification","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.nuclear_knot_classification","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/nuclear-knot-classification.lean#L58-L69","doc":"For `A = Z + N ≥ 4`, the nuclear braid closure is Borromean-like:\n`classifyByMassNumber (Z + N) = .borromean`.\n\nDerived from `hA` (the mass number selects the else-branch of\n`classifyByMassNumber`) — no longer the vacuous\n`∃ K, K = .borromean := ⟨.borromean, rfl⟩`, which held for any `A` and used\nnone of its hypotheses. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:nuclear-knot-classification","label":"conj:nuclear-knot-classification","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/nuclear-knot-classification.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.classifyByMassNumber","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.classifyByMassNumber","kind":"def","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/nuclear-knot-classification.lean#L50-L56","doc":"Classify a nuclear braid closure by mass number `A = Z + N`:\n`A ≤ 1` unknot, `A = 2` satellite, `A = 3` figure-eight, `A ≥ 4` Borromean. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.bindingScale","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.bindingScale","kind":"def","line":24,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/nuclear-knot-classification.lean#L24-L48","doc":"The binding scale α depends on the knot type through its volume.\n\n⚠ **CORRECTED 2026-08-30 (bean `qou-f8lit`).** Both Borromean entries read\n`7.327724753846269`, which is **wrong from digit 11** against\n`Vol(B₃) = 8·G = 7.327724753417752120…` (abs err `4.3e-10`). Every other Lean\ncarrier in the corpus — `building-block-knots.vol_borromean`,\n`categorical-neutron`, `categorical-proton` — already used `7.32772475341775`,\nso this file was the outlier, not an alternative convention.\n\nThe corpus had already IDENTIFIED this value as bad:\n`computations/snappy_borromean_volume.py` tabulates it as \"**wrong** at digit 11\".\nBut `docs/audits/2026-06-21-constant-consistency-axis2-clean.md` declared the axis\nCLEAN on the ground that it \"survives only as a *comment* in\n`experimental_constants.py`\" — while it was live here, in executable Lean, inside a\nmass formula, at two sites. That audit was evidently scoped to `computations/` and\nnever looked at `content/**/*.lean`.\n\nFound by `scripts/known-constant-literal-audit.py`, which compares literals to\ncomputed constants by VALUE rather than grepping for known-bad digit strings. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.instReprNuclearKnotType","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.instReprNuclearKnotType","kind":"instance","line":22,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/nuclear-knot-classification.lean#L22-L22","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.instReprNuclearKnotType.repr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.instReprNuclearKnotType.repr","kind":"def","line":22,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/nuclear-knot-classification.lean#L22-L22","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.instDecidableEqNuclearKnotType","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.instDecidableEqNuclearKnotType","kind":"instance","line":22,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/nuclear-knot-classification.lean#L22-L22","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.NuclearKnotType.borromean","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.NuclearKnotType.borromean","kind":"ctor","line":21,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/nuclear-knot-classification.lean#L21-L21","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.NuclearKnotType.figureEight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.NuclearKnotType.figureEight","kind":"ctor","line":20,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/nuclear-knot-classification.lean#L20-L20","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.NuclearKnotType.satellite","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.NuclearKnotType.satellite","kind":"ctor","line":19,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/nuclear-knot-classification.lean#L19-L19","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.NuclearKnotType.unknot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.NuclearKnotType.unknot","kind":"ctor","line":18,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/nuclear-knot-classification.lean#L18-L18","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.NuclearKnotType","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.NuclearKnotType","kind":"inductive","line":16,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/nuclear-knot-classification.lean#L16-L22","doc":"Classification of nuclear braid closures by knot type. ","signatureChunk":0}]}